NAME
    counters - tally per-address reads, writes, executes, and uninit reads

SYNOPSIS
    counters on <space>
    counters off
    counters clear
    counters <addr> [<len>]
    counters top [r|w|x|u] [<n>]
    counters cold <addr> <len>

DESCRIPTION
    Counts every read, write, execute, and uninitialized read per byte
    address in one selected memory space. Counting is off by default and
    arms against one memory space at a time.

    An address read before any write occurs while counting is armed is
    also tallied as an uninitialized read ('u'). Arm counting before the
    code path of interest runs so prior initialization is not miscounted.
    Execution counts track the processor's execution bus space; plain RAM
    spaces show zero executes unless code actually runs from RAM.

OPTIONS
    on <space>
        Start tallying accesses for memory space <space> (see spaces(1)).

    off
        Stop tallying while preserving collected counts for inspection.

    clear
        Reset all tallies to zero while remaining armed.

    <addr> [<len>]
        Print read, write, execute, and uninit totals across hex range
        <addr> for <len> bytes (default 1), plus how many bytes were
        touched.

    top [r|w|x|u] [<n>]
        Rank the <n> hottest addresses (default 20) by reads ('r',
        default), writes ('w'), executes ('x'), or uninitialized reads
        ('u').

    cold <addr> <len>
        List addresses in the hex range that were never accessed.

EXAMPLES
    counters on WRAM
    counters 13c6 8
    counters top w 10
    counters top u
    counters cold 1000 200
    counters off

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    watch(1), cov(1), bp(1), search(1), memfind(1), profile(1), spaces(1)
